WEBVTT

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.960
Okay, places, everyone.
Come on, come on. Get in position.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.240
Wait! I can't find my other eye.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.920
-All right, whose foot's in my face?
-It's mine. Give it back.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.680
You have saved our lives.
We are eternally grateful.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.840
(SHUSHING)

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.160
Buzz! Mind if I squeeze in next to ya?

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.320
Yes. No.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.200
(STAMMERING) I mean, why would
I mind squeezing next to you?

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.320
(CLEARING THROAT)

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.440
Is it hot in here?

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.600
Oh! Here they come!

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.240
Sarge, you got it?

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:33.680
Mission accomplished.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:34.960
REX: Hooray!

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.080
(LAUGHS)

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.200
Careful. Careful!

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:40.560
-JESSIE: Ooh!
-Oh!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.720
All right, guys. We got one shot at this.
Everyone ready?

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.600
We're ready, Woody. Let's do it!

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.840
Okay, Buzz. Make the call.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:53.840
(EXCLAIMS NERVOUSLY)

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.560
(RINGING)

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:03.000
BUZZ: Target is on approach.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.400
WOODY: Just like
we rehearsed it, guys.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:08.760
(PHONE CONTINUES RINGING)

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.040
Hello?

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.520
Hello? Anyone there?

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.360
(GROANS) Molly, stay out of my room!

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.560
MOLLY: I wasn't in your room.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.600
ANDY: Then who was messing
with my stuff?

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.040
MOLLY: It wasn't me.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.720
MR. POTATO HEAD:
Well, that went well.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.760
He held me! He actually held me!

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:47.800
HAMM: Oh, this is just sad.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.320
MR. POTATO HEAD: Who we kiddin'?
The kid's 17 years old.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.240
SLINKY: We ain't ever
gettin' played with.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.000
(SIGHS)

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.640
Guys, hey, hold up.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:00.400
We need a staff meeting.
Everyone! A staff meeting!

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.680
(GROANS) Not again!

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.240
Oh, come on.
Slink, gather everyone up.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.080
Uh, we are gathered, Woody.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.840
Okay. First off,

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:12.960
we all knew Operation Playtime
was a long shot.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.520
More like a misfire.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.560
But we've always said this job isn't
about getting played with. It's about...

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.760
Being there for Andy. We know.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.360
But we can try again! Right?

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.760
I'm callin' it, guys.
We're closing up shop.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.080
ALL: What?

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.400
Andy's going to college any day now.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.400
-That was our last shot.
-(UNHAPPILY) Oh.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.000
BUZZ: We're going
into attic mode, folks.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.960
Keep your accessories
with you at all times.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:39.040
Spare parts, batteries, anything
you need for an orderly transition.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.640
Orderly? Don't you get it? We're done!
Finished! Over the hill!

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.440
Hey, hey, hey, now. Come on, guys.
We all knew this day was coming.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.600
HAMM: Yeah, but now it's here.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.040
Look, every toy goes through this.
No one wants to see...

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.440
Hey, Sarge! What are you doing?

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.160
War's over, folks.
Me and the boys are moving on.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.280
-Moving on?
-You're going AWOL?

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.160
We done our duty. Andy's grown up.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.520
And let's face it,
when the trash bags come out,

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.280
we army guys are the first to go.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.880
-Trash bags?
-Who said anything about trash bags?

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.120
It has been an honor serving with you.
Good luck, folks.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.240
You're gonna need it.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.080
No, no, no. Wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.640
-(YELPS) We're getting thrown away?
-No. No one's getting thrown away.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.960
MR. POTATO HEAD:
How do you know?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.040
-(GASPING) We're being abandoned!
-We'll be fine, Jessie.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.480
-So why did Sarge leave?
-Should we leave?

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.840
-I thought we were goin' to the attic.
-Oh, I hate all this uncertainty!

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.880
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Hold on now. Wait a minute. Quiet!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.840
No one's getting thrown out, okay?
We're all still here.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.160
I mean, yeah,
we've lost friends along the way.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.840
-Wheezy and Etch and...
-Bo Peep?

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.280
Yeah. Even Bo.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.600
All good toys
who've gone on to new owners.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:52.360
But through every yard sale, every
spring cleaning, Andy held on to us!

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.840
He must care about us,
or we wouldn't be here.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.680
You wait. Andy's gonna tuck us in
the attic. It'll be safe and warm...

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.200
-And we'll all be together.
-Exactly!

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:05.120
There's games up there,
and books, and...

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.200
-The racecar track!
-The racecar track. Thank you!

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.680
-And the old TV.
-There you go, the old TV.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:15.880
And those guys from the Christmas
decorations box. They're fun, right?

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.360
-(MR. POTATO HEAD MUMBLES)
-Yeah.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.120
And someday, if we're lucky,
Andy may have kids of his own.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.760
And he'll play with us then, right?

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:25.560
We'll always be there for him.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:28.880
Come on, guys.
Let's get our parts together, get ready,

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.440
and go out on a high note.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.280
I'd better find my other eye.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.360
Where'd you leave it this time?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.520
Someplace dark. And dusty.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.000
Come on. Let's see how much
we're going for on eBay.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.680
Don't worry. Andy's gonna
take care of us. I guarantee it!

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.760
You guarantee it, huh?

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.880
I don't know, Buzz.
What else could I say?

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.640
Well, whatever happens,
at least we'll all be together.

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.040
WOODY: For infinity and beyond.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.760
MOLLY: Can I have your stereo?
ANDY: No.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.320
MOLLY: Why not?
ANDY: 'Cause I'm taking it with me.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.440
(GASPING)

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.360
-Can I have your computer?
-No.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.760
-Your video games?
-Forget it, Molly.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.600
Okay. Andy, let's get to work here.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.240
Anything you're not taking to college
either goes in the attic, or it's trash.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.320
-Mom, I'm not leaving till Friday.
-Come on. It's garbage day.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.240
-Mom.
-Look, it's simple.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.640
Skateboard, college.
Little League trophy, probably attic.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.200
Apple core, trash. You can do the rest.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.640
Why do you still have these toys?

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.760
(SIGHS) Molly, out of my room!

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.480
Three more days and it's mine!

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:04.040
Molly, you're not off the hook either.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.040
You have more toys
than you know what to do with.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:08.200
Some of them could make
other kids really happy.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.440
What kids?

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:12.640
The children at the daycare.
They're always asking for donations.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.760
-REX: What's daycare?
-(WOODY SHUSHING)

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.080
MOLLY: Mom.
ANDY'S MOM: No buts.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:18.360
You choose the toys you want to
donate, I'll drop them off at Sunnyside.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:19.840
(SIGHING)

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:31.360
JESSIE: Poor Barbie.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:32.680
HAMM: I get the Corvette.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.240
Andy, come on.
You need to start making decisions.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:36.360
Like what?

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.320
Like what are you gonna do
with these toys?

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.360
-Should we donate them to Sunnyside?
-No.

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:41.600
Maybe sell them online?

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.640
Mom, no one's gonna want
those old toys.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.600
They're junk.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.400
Fine. You have till Friday.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.200
Anything that's not packed for college
or in the attic

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.280
-is getting thrown out.
-(SIGHS) Whatever you say, Mom.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:56.080
(EXHALING)

